{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "fb1f784544e935c0",
      "x": -660,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 220,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# 🗺️ Using rheopy — the API in one picture\n\nThe rheopy way: **measure → data → model → fit → explore**.\n\nEach package does exactly one job, and they snap together: **rheodata** serves\ncurated datasets, **rheomodel** holds the constitutive equations, **rheofit** runs\nthe nonlinear regression, **rheolite** is the notebook + browser playground."
    },
    {
      "id": "a3a56658b42bfc5d",
      "x": -660,
      "y": 260,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 180,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 📦 Install\n\n```bash\npip install rheopy-rheodata rheopy-rheomodel rheofit\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "96810f5c73c339b7",
      "x": -660,
      "y": 480,
      "width": 600,
      "height": 360,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 🗃️ rheodata — data in\n\nCurated rheology datasets with provenance, measurement records, and citations.\n\n<div class=\"codeblock\"><span class=\"codelang\">python</span>\n<pre><code><span class=\"ck\">import</span> rheodata\n\nrheodata.<span class=\"cb\">list</span>()                             <span class=\"cc\"># every dataset, one row each</span>\nrheodata.search(material=<span class=\"cs\">\"carbopol\"</span>)        <span class=\"cc\"># substring filters</span>\nrheodata.info(<span class=\"cs\">\"caggioni_pg_carbopol_2pct\"</span>)  <span class=\"cc\"># summary + DOI link</span>\n\nds = rheodata.load(<span class=\"cs\">\"caggioni_pg_carbopol_2pct\"</span>)\nds.df.head()                                <span class=\"cc\"># tidy DataFrame</span>\nrheodata.plot(<span class=\"cs\">\"caggioni_pg_carbopol_2pct\"</span>)   <span class=\"cc\"># figure</span></code></pre>\n</div>\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "f2ff0fcea69f57a8",
      "x": -20,
      "y": 480,
      "width": 600,
      "height": 360,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 🧮 rheomodel — pick a model\n\nNine flow-curve models as pure functions — equations, bounds, verified citations.\n\n- **Yield stress:** `herschel_bulkley`, `bingham`, `casson`\n- **Microstructure-informed:** `tc`, `tc_carreau`, `tccc`\n- **No yield stress:** `power_law`, `carreau`, `carreau_carreau`\n\n<div class=\"codeblock\"><span class=\"codelang\">python</span>\n<pre><code><span class=\"ck\">import</span> rheomodel\n\nhb = rheomodel.get_model(<span class=\"cs\">\"herschel_bulkley\"</span>)\nsigma = hb.equation(gamma_dot, sigma_y=<span class=\"cn\">20.0</span>, K=<span class=\"cn\">10.0</span>, n=<span class=\"cn\">0.6</span>)\n<span class=\"cc\"># hb.CITATION - hb.PARAM_INFO - hb.get_equation_latex()</span></code></pre>\n</div>\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "a8c7d92ace6a54c6",
      "x": -660,
      "y": 880,
      "width": 600,
      "height": 240,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 🔧 The bridge — data → fit\n\n<div class=\"codeblock\"><span class=\"codelang\">python</span>\n<pre><code>df = rheodata.to_rheofit(<span class=\"cs\">\"caggioni_pg_carbopol_2pct\"</span>,\n                         sample=<span class=\"cs\">\"carbopol_2pct\"</span>)\n<span class=\"cc\"># -&gt; \"Shear rate / 1/s\" and \"Stress / Pa\",</span>\n<span class=\"cc\">#    exactly what rheofit.fit expects</span></code></pre>\n</div>\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "06a559b79feb43c4",
      "x": -660,
      "y": 1160,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 300,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 🎯 rheofit — fit\n\nNonlinear regression: physics-informed starts, ladder seeding, multi-start\nglobal search (`effort`: fast / normal / thorough).\n\n<div class=\"codeblock\"><span class=\"codelang\">python</span>\n<pre><code><span class=\"ck\">import</span> rheofit\n\nres = rheofit.fit(df, <span class=\"cs\">\"carreau_carreau\"</span>, effort=<span class=\"cs\">\"thorough\"</span>, seed=<span class=\"cn\">0</span>)\n<span class=\"cc\"># res.params - fitted values with uncertainties</span></code></pre>\n</div>\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "314f0869e8915120",
      "x": -660,
      "y": 1500,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 200,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## 🔬 Explore — rheolite\n\nNotebooks, the browser fit app, and the interactive model explorers.\n\n🌊 [Fit app](https://rheopy.github.io/rheofit/) — upload data or pick a rheodata\ndataset, choose a model, fit in the browser · 📓 [rheolite](https://github.com/rheopy/rheolite)"
    },
    {
      "id": "9e8dbf1d41573904",
      "x": -660,
      "y": 1740,
      "width": 600,
      "height": 100,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "[← back to the rheopy ecosystem](https://rheopy.github.io/canvas/)"
    },
    {
      "id": "153188446d49dcd6",
